  "releaseNotes": "v0.8.0: record counts, for example to show import progress. IDkPlusQuery<T>.CountAsync asks DK Plus how many records match the query; customers and products use GET /api/v1/Customer/info/count and /api/v1/Product/info/count with the same filters as the page query, normalized the same way (the product modified-since filter is sent as modified, as on the page). A filter the count endpoint lacks (customer ForName and ForEmail; product ForIdentifier, ForAliasItemCode and Deleted) throws NotSupportedException naming it before any request, rather than counting a wider set; Take caps the count, and the projection and page size do not affect it. A body that is not an integer is a DkPlusContractException. Purchase.Vendor.Query().CountAsync() reads the change count of the dkERP vendor table APVEND (GET /api/v1/general/table/apvend/changes, an object {\"Count\": n}); with no modified time it is the total row count, which includes rows without a vendor number that the vendor list skips, so it is an upper bound of the vendors listed (verified live on 2026-10-27: 384 counted, 383 listed plus 1 skipped). ModifiedSince is sent as the table's modified parameter; any other vendor filter throws NotSupportedException. IDkPlusQuery<T> gains CountAsync (Task<long>, a default interface member, so existing implementations keep working; it throws NotSupportedException where the portable count is null); Customer.Group.Query() and Product.Group.Query() keep their v0.7 return types and count the dkERP group tables ARGROUPS and INGROUPS the same way. New: Purchase.Vendor.Group (IDkPlusVendorGroupResource) reads vendor groups as the DK-specific VendorGroup model from the dkERP table APGROUPS (GROUPID, DESCRIPTION, RECORDMODIFIED only) through the generic table read, with ModifiedSince; its CountAsync counts APGROUPS, so client.Purchase.Vendor.Group.Query().ModifiedSince(since).CountAsync() works. Fixed: Table.GetRecordsAsync without a maximum was previously capped at 200 rows (the DK Plus default when count is omitted); it now asks for the table's change count plus a margin, re-reads up to three times when a result fills it and then throws InvalidOperationException, warns (event TableReadIncomplete, 1005) when fewer rows arrive than the count, sends count=10000 for a key-filtered read, and reads number and boolean cells as invariant text (an array or object cell is a DkPlusContractException); a maximum below 1 throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException. Project delete goes through the table resource. Every 0.7.1 member keeps its signature, and new interface members are default members, so code compiled against 0.7.1 still loads. Vendor groups and the vendor and group counts are read through the table resource. Group counts apply only ModifiedSince (the table's modified parameter). The portable IErpQuery.CountAsync (DevOp.ERP.Abstractions 0.8.0) returns the same counts for customers, products and vendors, and null where the DK Plus count would throw or no count exists.",
